From 8262ab7a32f9943b85b543ae5b8748c1b33f8405 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 08:00:45 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 055/122] R2004 DWG: write the file container as AutoCAD, with
 LZ77 compression

The R2004 container (also the frame of R2010+) was written so that no
reader accepted it: ACadSharp failed on duplicate empty section names
(the section map and page map were listed as data sections), and the
pages had wrong sizes, the Preview a page of 1.3 MB, unaligned system
pages and a clobbered tail of the file header.

* src/encode.c (encode_r2004_container): New, replaces the old section
map/page map writer. As AutoCAD's own R2004 files: the empty section
first, ids counting down in the section map order; compressed sections in
0x7400 pages, the others in one page of their size rounded up to 0x80
(Preview 0x400); page headers with page size, 64-bit start offset, header
and data checksums; pages aligned to 0x20 and padded with the magic
sequence; the section map and the page map numbered 2 after the data
pages, each followed by the blank header copy; the file header at 0x80
with the magic bytes up to 0x100, repeated at the end; the AppInfo and
AppInfoHistory addresses at 0x2C and 0x30.
(r2004_compress): New LZ77 compressor (ODA 4.7), with hash chains. Every
stream starts with a literal length, the only first form decode.c reads.
(copy_R2004_section, store_R2004_section, compress_R2004_section) and
the unused helpers: Remove.
* src/encode2.c: Remove the unused HAVE_COMPRESS_R2004_SECTION.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
